    <property name="text">
     <string>Output(=switch, relays, ...) address should be in the range: 1...1024.  An output address will roughly be divided by 4 to calculate the Decoder's address (which is stored in CV1 and CV9), as well as the RS-Bus address (which is stored in CV10).  Uninitialised Switch decoders listen to loco address 6999. If the SET button is pushed, a PoM write message is send to this address, and CV1, CV9 and CV10 will be set.  Note that, as a result of the mapping between Switch and Decoder addresses, Output addresses will remapped to: 1, 5, 9, 13 ... 1021.</string>
    </property>
